8. LAYOUT DETAILS

- Use the existing application font and shared controls.
- Use clean, aligned form fields and consistent spacing.
- Use subtle card borders, restrained shadows, and 8px corner radii where
  consistent with existing components.
- Keep readiness issues directly below Calculation Context.
- Keep live stage details directly below the execution stepper.
- Place Outputs and Execution History below the execution details.
- On smaller screens, stack controls and cards and allow the stepper to
  wrap or scroll without truncating labels.

9. IMPLEMENTATION RULES

- Inspect the existing Calculation module before implementing changes.
- Reuse shared components, services, routing patterns, and theme tokens.
- Preserve existing calculation identifiers and API contracts.
- Never enable execution before readiness passes for the current selection.
- Never reuse readiness approval across different selections.
- Never allow duplicate execution for the same active context.
- Clearly distinguish readiness failures from execution failures.
- Show the currently running stage and task using actual backend status.
- Treat readiness failure, ready-to-run, running, failed, and completed as
  distinct UI states.
- Do not display contradictory states simultaneously.
- If an integration is unavailable, clearly identify the missing backend
  dependency rather than presenting simulated success as real execution.
- Keep sample data restricted to explicitly labeled development/demo mode.
